{"meta": {"limit": 500, "next": null, "offset": 0, "previous": null, "total_count": 20}, "objects": [{"acronym": "iab", "ad": null, "charter": null, "comments": "1st meeting at 35th IETF - Los Angeles, CA - March 1996", "description": "The Internet Architecture Board provides long-range technical direction for Internet development, ensuring the Internet continues to grow and evolve as a platform for global communication and innovation.\r\n\r\nIn its work, the IAB strives to:\r\n\r\n- Ensure that the Internet is a trusted medium of communication that provides a solid technical foundation for privacy and security, especially in light of pervasive surveillance,\r\n- Establish the technical direction for an Internet that will enable billions more people to connect, support the vision for an Internet of Things, and allow mobile networks to flourish, while keeping the core capabilities that have been a foundation of the Internet’s success, and\r\n- Promote the technical evolution of an open Internet without special controls, especially those which hinder trust in the network.\r\n\r\nThe IAB is responsible for:\r\n\r\n- Providing architectural oversight of Internet protocols and procedures\r\n- Liaising with other organizations on behalf of the Internet Engineering Task Force (IETF)\r\n- Reviewing appeals of the Internet standards process\r\n- Managing Internet standards documents (the RFC series) and protocol parameter value assignment\r\n- Confirming the Chair of the IETF and the IETF Area Directors\r\n- Selecting the Internet Research Task Force (IRTF) Chair\r\n- Acting as source of advice and guidance to the Internet Society\r\n\r\nThe IAB convenes workshops of specialists, initiates and executes specific work programs, and writes documents that lead to comprehensive technical analyses of matters of interest. While its work may influence the industry broadly, the IAB does not operate from a grand-architecture blueprint of, or vision for, the Internet. Rather, the IAB’s efforts are guided by fundamental design principles—the Internet’s building blocks and their interactions—that make the global open Internet what it is. The IAB also helps connect different fields of expertise when this is needed to understand the full situation affecting the evolution of the Internet. For instance technology, policy and other considerations often impact each other.\r\n\r\nThe IAB is comprised of 13 members who serve as individuals, and not as representatives of any company, agency, or other organization. The IAB is chartered both as a committee of the IETF and an advisory body of the Internet Society. Further details about the IAB are documented in RFC 2850.", "id": 7, "list_archive": "", "list_email": "iab@iab.org", "list_subscribe": "", "meeting_seen_as_area": false, "name": "Internet Architecture Board", "parent": "/api/v1/group/group/1/", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/group/group/7/", "state": "/api/v1/name/groupstatename/active/", "time": "2026-05-05T05:53:14Z", "type": "/api/v1/name/grouptypename/ietf/", "unused_states": [], "unused_tags": [], "used_roles": "['chair', 'delegate', 'exofficio', 'liaison', 'liaison_coordinator', 'member']", "uses_milestone_dates": false}, {"acronym": "nmrg", "ad": null, "charter": "/api/v1/doc/document/charter-irtf-nmrg/", "comments": "", "description": "The Network Management Research Group (NMRG) provides a forum for\nresearchers to explore new technologies for the management of the Internet.\nIn particular, the NMRG will work on solutions for problems that are not\nyet considered well understood enough for engineering work within the IETF.", "id": 38, "list_archive": "https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/browse/nmrg", "list_email": "nmrg@irtf.org", "list_subscribe": "https://mailman.irtf.org/mailman/listinfo/nmrg", "meeting_seen_as_area": false, "name": "Network Management", "parent": "/api/v1/group/group/3/", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/group/group/38/", "state": "/api/v1/name/groupstatename/active/", "time": "2025-11-06T17:55:27Z", "type": "/api/v1/name/grouptypename/rg/", "unused_states": [], "unused_tags": [], "used_roles": "[]", "uses_milestone_dates": true}, {"acronym": "dhc", "ad": null, "charter": "/api/v1/doc/document/charter-ietf-dhc/", "comments": "", "description": "The Dynamic Host Configuration Working Group (DHC WG) has developed DHCP\nfor automated allocation, configuration and management of IP addresses,\nIPv6 prefixes, IP protocol stack and other parameters. DHCPv4 is\ncurrently a Draft Standard and is documented in RFC 2131 and RFC 2132.\nDHCPv6 is currently a Proposed Standard and is being updated. The WG\nplans to advance the DHCPv6 protocol to Internet standard.", "id": 988, "list_archive": "https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/browse/dhcwg/", "list_email": "dhcwg@ietf.org", "list_subscribe": "http://www.ietf.org/mailman/listinfo/dhcwg", "meeting_seen_as_area": false, "name": "Dynamic Host Configuration", "parent": "/api/v1/group/group/1052/", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/group/group/988/", "state": "/api/v1/name/groupstatename/active/", "time": "2026-10-05T16:19:57Z", "type": "/api/v1/name/grouptypename/wg/", "unused_states": [], "unused_tags": [], "used_roles": "[]", "uses_milestone_dates": true}, {"acronym": "gen", "ad": null, "charter": null, "comments": "", "description": "The General Area (GEN) consists of WGs and other activities focused on supporting, updating and maintaining the IETF standards development process. These non-WG activities include the General Area Open Meeting (GENAREA), General Area Review Team (Gen-ART) and other IETF-wide teams.\r\n\r\nGEN also has non-working group mailing lists to support the discussion of the policies and procedures of the IETF standards process.  These topic-focused lists include:\r\n\r\n* AI use in the IETF standards process - `ai-in-standards <https://mailman3.ietf.org/mailman3/lists/ai-in-standards.ietf.org/>`_\r\n* Antitrust - `antitrust-policy <https://mailman3.ietf.org/mailman3/lists/antitrust-policy.ietf.org>`_\r\n* Intellectual Property - `ipr-wg <https://mailman3.ietf.org/mailman3/lists/ipr-wg.ietf.org>`_\r\n* Meeting venues - `mtgvenue <https://mailman3.ietf.org/mailman3/lists/mtgvenue.ietf.org>`_\r\n* Moderation - `mod-discuss <https://mailman3.ietf.org/mailman3/lists/mod-discuss.ietf.org/>`_\r\n* NomCom - `ietf-nomcom <https://mailman3.ietf.org/mailman3/lists/ietf-nomcom.ietf.org/>`_", "id": 1008, "list_archive": "", "list_email": "", "list_subscribe": "", "meeting_seen_as_area": false, "name": "General Area", "parent": "/api/v1/group/group/2/", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/group/group/1008/", "state": "/api/v1/name/groupstatename/active/", "time": "2026-09-15T18:43:11Z", "type": "/api/v1/name/grouptypename/area/", "unused_states": [], "unused_tags": [], "used_roles": "[]", "uses_milestone_dates": false}, {"acronym": "none", "ad": null, "charter": null, "comments": "This is here so that 'none' can be entered in, for example, idform.", "description": "No description available", "id": 1027, "list_archive": "", "list_email": "", "list_subscribe": "", "meeting_seen_as_area": false, "name": "Individual Submissions", "parent": "/api/v1/group/group/1008/", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/group/group/1027/", "state": "/api/v1/name/groupstatename/active/", "time": "2024-03-20T08:30:40Z", "type": "/api/v1/name/grouptypename/individ/", "unused_states": [], "unused_tags": [], "used_roles": "[]", "uses_milestone_dates": false}, {"acronym": "idr", "ad": null, "charter": "/api/v1/doc/document/charter-ietf-idr/", "comments": "This working group resulted from BGP and IPIDRP merging.", "description": "The Border Gateway Protocol (BGP) (version 4) [RFC4271] was originally developed to support inter-domain IP routing over the Internet and other IP-based networks. The introduction of multiprotocol extensions [RFC4760] enabled BGP to support multiple address families, significantly broadening its applicability to a wide range of routing features and deployment scenarios.", "id": 1041, "list_archive": "https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/browse/idr/", "list_email": "idr@ietf.org", "list_subscribe": "https://www.ietf.org/mailman/listinfo/idr", "meeting_seen_as_area": false, "name": "Inter-Domain Routing", "parent": "/api/v1/group/group/1249/", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/group/group/1041/", "state": "/api/v1/name/groupstatename/active/", "time": "2025-03-19T10:55:28Z", "type": "/api/v1/name/grouptypename/wg/", "unused_states": [], "unused_tags": [], "used_roles": "[]", "uses_milestone_dates": true}, {"acronym": "fax", "ad": null, "charter": "/api/v1/doc/document/charter-ietf-fax/", "comments": "1st meeting at 37th IETF - San Jose, CA", "description": "Previous IETF efforts developed specifications for simple and extended\r\nInternet mail-based facsimile service profiles, tailored to interwork \r\nwith the world of T.30 facsimile.  This extension effort will take care \r\nof differential routing between classic Internet mail and timely \r\ndeliveries, and consider with particular regard universal messaging \r\nissues and its relation with Internet mail.", "id": 1054, "list_archive": "http://www.imc.org/ietf-fax/", "list_email": "ietf-fax@imc.org", "list_subscribe": "ietf-fax-request@imc.org", "meeting_seen_as_area": false, "name": "Internet Fax", "parent": "/api/v1/group/group/934/", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/group/group/1054/", "state": "/api/v1/name/groupstatename/conclude/", "time": "2011-12-09T20:00:00Z", "type": "/api/v1/name/grouptypename/wg/", "unused_states": [], "unused_tags": [], "used_roles": "[]", "uses_milestone_dates": true}, {"acronym": "secsh", "ad": null, "charter": "/api/v1/doc/document/charter-ietf-secsh/", "comments": "", "description": "\nThe goal of the working group is to update and standardize the popular\r\nSSH protocol. SSH provides support for secure remote login, secure file\r\ntransfer, and secure TCP/IP and X11 forwardings. It can automatically\r\nencrypt, authenticate, and compress transmitted data.  The working\r\ngroup will attempt to assure that the SSH protocol", "id": 1259, "list_archive": "ftp://ftp.ietf.org/ietf-mail-archive/secsh/", "list_email": "ietf-ssh@netbsd.org", "list_subscribe": "majordomo@netbsd.org", "meeting_seen_as_area": false, "name": "Secure Shell", "parent": "/api/v1/group/group/1260/", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/group/group/1259/", "state": "/api/v1/name/groupstatename/conclude/", "time": "2011-12-09T20:00:00Z", "type": "/api/v1/name/grouptypename/wg/", "unused_states": [], "unused_tags": [], "used_roles": "[]", "uses_milestone_dates": true}, {"acronym": "agentx", "ad": null, "charter": "/api/v1/doc/document/charter-ietf-agentx/", "comments": "Old email archive at: ftp://ftp.ietf.org/ietf-mail-archive/agentx/", "description": "The goal of this working group is to define standards-track technology\r\nfor SNMP Agent extensibility.  The resulting technology specification\r\nwill allow independently developed sub-agents to communicate with a\r\nmaster-agent running on an Internet device.", "id": 1282, "list_archive": "https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/browse/agentx/", "list_email": "agentx@ietf.org", "list_subscribe": "https://www.ietf.org/mailman/listinfo/agentx", "meeting_seen_as_area": false, "name": "SNMP Agent Extensibility", "parent": "/api/v1/group/group/1193/", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/group/group/1282/", "state": "/api/v1/name/groupstatename/conclude/", "time": "2011-12-09T20:00:00Z", "type": "/api/v1/name/grouptypename/wg/", "unused_states": [], "unused_tags": [], "used_roles": "[]", "uses_milestone_dates": true}, {"acronym": "tpix", "ad": null, "charter": "/api/v1/doc/document/charter-ietf-tpix/", "comments": "Not really concluded. tpix was changed to catnip", "description": "\tTP/IX is a new version of the IP, TCP, and UDP protocols, to\n\tadvance the Internet technology to the scale and performance of\n\tthe next generation of internetwork technology. TP/IX has been\n\tassigned the IP version number 7.", "id": 1317, "list_archive": "world.std.com:~/pub/tpix/*", "list_email": "tpix@world.std.com", "list_subscribe": "tpix-request@world.std.com", "meeting_seen_as_area": false, "name": "TP/IX", "parent": "/api/v1/group/group/1052/", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/group/group/1317/", "state": "/api/v1/name/groupstatename/conclude/", "time": "2011-12-09T20:00:00Z", "type": "/api/v1/name/grouptypename/wg/", "unused_states": [], "unused_tags": [], "used_roles": "[]", "uses_milestone_dates": true}, {"acronym": "tsv", "ad": null, "charter": null, "comments": "", "description": "The transport and services area - usually just called \"transport area\" or \"TSV area\" - covers a range of technical topics related to data transport in the Internet.\r\n\r\nThe Transport Area works on mechanisms related to end-to-end data transport to support Internet applications and services that exchange potentially large volumes of traffic at potentially high bandwidths. A key focus are mechanisms to detect and react to congestion in the Internet, such as the congestion control algorithms in Internet transport control protocols such as TCP, SCTP, and DCCP, as well as congestion management schemes such as PCN and CONEX.\r\n\r\nCurrent and new transport work includes congestion signaling and reporting, forward error correction, multicast, QoS and reservation signaling, DiffServ? and congestion control for unresponsive flows, NAT regularization and specification, storage protocols for the Internet, peer-to-peer streaming, performance metrics for Internet paths, experimentation with congestion control schemes developed in the IRTF, multipath extensions to existing transport protocols, congestion control for \"background\" bulk transfers, and extensions to the IETF protocols for multimedia transport.\r\n\r\nThe transport area intersects most frequently with Internet area, the applications area, the RAI area, the security area and several IRTF research groups.", "id": 1324, "list_archive": "", "list_email": "", "list_subscribe": "", "meeting_seen_as_area": false, "name": "Transport Area", "parent": "/api/v1/group/group/2/", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/group/group/1324/", "state": "/api/v1/name/groupstatename/conclude/", "time": "2023-04-21T21:47:13Z", "type": "/api/v1/name/grouptypename/area/", "unused_states": [], "unused_tags": [], "used_roles": "[]", "uses_milestone_dates": false}, {"acronym": "tsvwg", "ad": null, "charter": "/api/v1/doc/document/charter-ietf-tsvwg/", "comments": "", "description": "The Transport and Services Working Group (TSVWG) is the forum for development and  publication of RFCs dealing with transport-layer topics that are not in scope of an existing working group or do not justify the formation of a new working group.", "id": 1463, "list_archive": "https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/browse/tsvwg/", "list_email": "tsvwg@ietf.org", "list_subscribe": "https://www.ietf.org/mailman/listinfo/tsvwg", "meeting_seen_as_area": false, "name": "Transport and Services Working Group", "parent": "/api/v1/group/group/2412/", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/group/group/1463/", "state": "/api/v1/name/groupstatename/active/", "time": "2025-03-21T02:28:30Z", "type": "/api/v1/name/grouptypename/wg/", "unused_states": [], "unused_tags": [], "used_roles": "[]", "uses_milestone_dates": true}, {"acronym": "ipoib", "ad": null, "charter": "/api/v1/doc/document/charter-ietf-ipoib/", "comments": "1st meeting at 50th IETF-Minneapolis, MN\r\nwith the acronym of infinib (IP over InfiniBand plus MIBS", "description": "\nE-mail archive: \r\nhttp://www.ietf.org/mail-archive/working-groups/ipoverib/current/mailli\r\nst.html", "id": 1539, "list_archive": "https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/browse/ipoverib", "list_email": "ipoverib@ietf.org", "list_subscribe": "ipoverib-request@ietf.org", "meeting_seen_as_area": false, "name": "IP over InfiniBand", "parent": "/api/v1/group/group/1052/", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/group/group/1539/", "state": "/api/v1/name/groupstatename/conclude/", "time": "2011-12-09T20:00:00Z", "type": "/api/v1/name/grouptypename/wg/", "unused_states": [], "unused_tags": [], "used_roles": "[]", "uses_milestone_dates": true}, {"acronym": "dime", "ad": null, "charter": "/api/v1/doc/document/charter-ietf-dime/", "comments": "", "description": "The Diameter Maintenance and Extensions WG will focus on maintenance and \nextensions to the Diameter protocol required to enable its use for \nauthentication, authorization, accounting, charging in network access, \nprovisioning of configuration information within the network, and for \nnew AAA session management uses within the extensibility rules of the \nDiameter base protocol.", "id": 1682, "list_archive": "https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/browse/dime/", "list_email": "dime@ietf.org", "list_subscribe": "https://www.ietf.org/mailman/listinfo/dime", "meeting_seen_as_area": false, "name": "Diameter Maintenance and Extensions", "parent": "/api/v1/group/group/1193/", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/group/group/1682/", "state": "/api/v1/name/groupstatename/conclude/", "time": "2024-03-14T03:56:36Z", "type": "/api/v1/name/grouptypename/wg/", "unused_states": [], "unused_tags": [], "used_roles": "[]", "uses_milestone_dates": true}, {"acronym": "rai", "ad": null, "charter": null, "comments": "", "description": "No description available", "id": 1683, "list_archive": "", "list_email": "", "list_subscribe": "", "meeting_seen_as_area": false, "name": "Real-time Applications and Infrastructure Area", "parent": "/api/v1/group/group/2/", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/group/group/1683/", "state": "/api/v1/name/groupstatename/conclude/", "time": "2015-06-02T16:03:02Z", "type": "/api/v1/name/grouptypename/area/", "unused_states": [], "unused_tags": [], "used_roles": "[]", "uses_milestone_dates": false}, {"acronym": "roll", "ad": null, "charter": "/api/v1/doc/document/charter-ietf-roll/", "comments": "", "description": "Low-power and Lossy Networks (LLNs ) are made up of many embedded\ndevices with limited power, memory, and processing resources. They are\ninterconnected by a variety of links, such as IEEE 802.15.4, Bluetooth,\nLow Power Wi-Fi, wired or other low-power PLC (Powerline Communication)\nlinks. LLNs are transitioning to an end-to-end IP-based solution to\navoid the problem of non-interoperable networks interconnected by\nprotocol translation gateways and proxies.", "id": 1730, "list_archive": "https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/browse/roll/", "list_email": "roll@ietf.org", "list_subscribe": "http://www.ietf.org/mailman/listinfo/roll", "meeting_seen_as_area": false, "name": "Routing Over Low power and Lossy networks", "parent": "/api/v1/group/group/1249/", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/group/group/1730/", "state": "/api/v1/name/groupstatename/active/", "time": "2025-03-19T10:58:05Z", "type": "/api/v1/name/grouptypename/wg/", "unused_states": [], "unused_tags": [], "used_roles": "[]", "uses_milestone_dates": true}, {"acronym": "appsawg", "ad": null, "charter": "/api/v1/doc/document/charter-ietf-appsawg/", "comments": "", "description": "\n  The Applications Area sometimes receives proposals for the development\n  of specifications dealing with application-related topics that are not\n  in scope for an existing working group and do not justify the formation\n  of a new working group.", "id": 1805, "list_archive": "https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/browse/art", "list_email": "art@ietf.org", "list_subscribe": "https://www.ietf.org/mailman/listinfo/art", "meeting_seen_as_area": false, "name": "ART Area General Applications Working Group", "parent": "/api/v1/group/group/2010/", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/group/group/1805/", "state": "/api/v1/name/groupstatename/conclude/", "time": "2017-07-06T22:15:13Z", "type": "/api/v1/name/grouptypename/wg/", "unused_states": [], "unused_tags": [], "used_roles": "[]", "uses_milestone_dates": true}, {"acronym": "6tisch", "ad": null, "charter": "/api/v1/doc/document/charter-ietf-6tisch/", "comments": "", "description": "6TiSCH: \"IPv6 over the TSCH mode of IEEE 802.15.4e\".", "id": 1903, "list_archive": "https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/browse/6tisch/", "list_email": "6tisch@ietf.org", "list_subscribe": "https://www.ietf.org/mailman/listinfo/6tisch", "meeting_seen_as_area": false, "name": "IPv6 over the TSCH mode of IEEE 802.15.4e", "parent": "/api/v1/group/group/1052/", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/group/group/1903/", "state": "/api/v1/name/groupstatename/conclude/", "time": "2023-07-19T15:10:48Z", "type": "/api/v1/name/grouptypename/wg/", "unused_states": [], "unused_tags": [], "used_roles": "[]", "uses_milestone_dates": true}, {"acronym": "wimse", "ad": null, "charter": "/api/v1/doc/document/charter-ietf-wimse/", "comments": "", "description": "Background & Motivation", "id": 2404, "list_archive": "https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/browse/wimse/", "list_email": "wimse@ietf.org", "list_subscribe": "https://www.ietf.org/mailman/listinfo/wimse", "meeting_seen_as_area": false, "name": "Workload Identity in Multi System Environments", "parent": "/api/v1/group/group/2010/", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/group/group/2404/", "state": "/api/v1/name/groupstatename/active/", "time": "2026-03-18T09:57:12Z", "type": "/api/v1/name/grouptypename/wg/", "unused_states": [], "unused_tags": [], "used_roles": "[]", "uses_milestone_dates": true}, {"acronym": "sshm", "ad": null, "charter": "/api/v1/doc/document/charter-ietf-sshm/", "comments": "", "description": "The main goal of the working group is to maintain the Secure Shell (SSH) protocol. SSH provides support for secure remote login, file transfer, and forwarding UNIX-domain sockets, TCP/IP and X11. It can automatically encrypt, authenticate, and compress transmitted data.", "id": 2430, "list_archive": "https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/browse/ssh/", "list_email": "ssh@ietf.org", "list_subscribe": "https://mailman3.ietf.org/mailman3/lists/ssh.ietf.org/", "meeting_seen_as_area": false, "name": "Secure Shell Maintenance", "parent": "/api/v1/group/group/1260/", "resource_uri": "/api/v1/group/group/2430/", "state": "/api/v1/name/groupstatename/active/", "time": "2024-09-27T18:23:55Z", "type": "/api/v1/name/grouptypename/wg/", "unused_states": [], "unused_tags": [], "used_roles": "[]", "uses_milestone_dates": true}]}